1 NOTE Very strongly identified as the son of William Charles Shafe and Flore
2 CONC nce Louisa Webster. His 1893 Walworth baptism names Charles William an
2 CONC d Florence Louisa Shafe; the 1901 census records Harry C. as their son
2 CONC . His 1911 marriage instead names his father as Henry Charles Shafe, b
2 CONC ox maker, probably a forename error because the occupation matches Wil
2 CONC liam and the groom himself was Henry Charles. Served in the Royal Fiel
2 CONC d Artillery during the First World War and was discharged in Glasgow o
2 CONC n 10 January 1918 as no longer physically fit. Service description: 5 
2 CONC ft 10 in, blue eyes, brown hair, tattoos on both arms; described as st
2 CONC eady, solid and industrious. Occupation on marriage: porter.
