1 NOTE Recorded in 1861 as John Shafe's son, aged 15, born Bury St Edmunds, a
2 CONC nd working as a copper-plate polisher. From 1871 to 1891 he is traceab
2 CONC le in Newington with wife Mary, later as a box maker; records alternat
2 CONC e between Shafe and Shape. This continuity makes the link to John very
2 CONC  strong. His specialised 1861 metalworking occupation is a legitimate 
2 CONC clue when investigating a possible connection to the earlier London co
2 CONC pper-plate manufacturer John Shafe, but it does not by itself establis
2 CONC h that relationship.
